Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [guacr-database is a private-dependency dead branch never activated by this wheel's own Cargo feature set]

crates/webrtc-bindings/Cargo.toml (the maturin build target) depends on
keeper-pam-webrtc-rs with default-features = false and features = ["python-support"]
only, which never enables "builtin-handlers" and therefore never pulls in the
optional "guacr" dependency, let alone guacr's own optional "database" feature.
That shape is fixed in the published crate's own manifest, not something we are
changing: the officially released wheel is built the same way.

guacr-database is nonetheless a `[workspace]` member, and its mandatory (non-optional)
dependency keeperdb-core/keeperdb-drivers is a git dependency on
https://github.com/Keeper-Security/keeperdb (branch "release", pinned to a specific
commit) which is a private repository outside Keeper Security's org — 401 Unauthorized
for anyone else, including this CI. Because Cargo resolves every workspace member's
manifest (including unreached optional dependencies) to build a single workspace-wide
Cargo.lock, just being a workspace member is enough to make `cargo` try to clone that
private repo and fail, even though nothing in the actual compiled extension ever
references it.

Dropping the guacr-database path dependency (and the "database"/"dynamodb" features
that gate it) removes the only reachable-at-resolution-time edge into those private
repos, without touching anything the published wheel actually compiles: guacr-database
was never part of this crate's build graph to begin with.

The same root Cargo.toml also carries a `[patch.crates-io] tiberius = { git =
"https://github.com/Keeper-Security/tiberius", ... }` override for the mssql driver
keeperdb-drivers would otherwise pull in — equally private, equally unreachable, and
now provably dead (dropping guacr-database already makes it "not used in the crate
graph" per cargo's own warning). Drop it too rather than leave an inert pointer at a
repo we cannot resolve.

--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@
 [workspace]
-members = ["crates/keeper-pam-webrtc-rs", "crates/webrtc-bindings", "crates/guacr", "crates/guacr-encoder", "crates/guacr-handlers", "crates/guacr-protocol", "crates/guacr-terminal", "crates/guacr-ssh", "crates/guacr-telnet", "crates/guacr-rdp", "crates/guacr-vnc", "crates/guacr-database", "crates/guacr-sftp", "crates/guacr-rbi", "crates/guacr-threat-detection", "crates/guacr-tn3270", "crates/guacr-tn5250", "crates/guacr-recording", "crates/guacr-recorder", "crates/guacr-guacd", "crates/pam-socks5"]
+members = ["crates/keeper-pam-webrtc-rs", "crates/webrtc-bindings", "crates/guacr", "crates/guacr-encoder", "crates/guacr-handlers", "crates/guacr-protocol", "crates/guacr-terminal", "crates/guacr-ssh", "crates/guacr-telnet", "crates/guacr-rdp", "crates/guacr-vnc", "crates/guacr-sftp", "crates/guacr-rbi", "crates/guacr-threat-detection", "crates/guacr-tn3270", "crates/guacr-tn5250", "crates/guacr-recording", "crates/guacr-recorder", "crates/guacr-guacd", "crates/pam-socks5"]
 resolver = "2"

 [workspace.package]
@@ -128,13 +128,6 @@
 webpki-roots = "1.0"
 pyo3-log = "0.13.4"

-[patch.crates-io]
-# tiberius: match the fork keeperdb-driver-mssql is authored against. Keeper's fork
-# patches cross-platform NTLM (AuthMethod::windows on unix, prisma/tiberius#408) which
-# our old vendor/tiberius copy lacked. Must live in the ROOT [patch] because the root
-# workspace patch is the only one that applies to path-dep keeperdb crates.
-tiberius = { git = "https://github.com/Keeper-Security/tiberius", rev = "f012b7948be64dcc95d2a6d3f8db8dd7e8a916b2" }
-
 [profile.dev]
 incremental = false

